  [case id=bus-038-fire-order-byte-exact-3-subscribers level=core gate=enforced
  [tags bus emit fire-order priority tie registration-order byte-exact hostile]
  [doc [#
HOSTILE (major): the existing fire-order fixtures assert only the COUNT or the
FIRST fired subscription, so a tie-scramble (two subscribers at equal priority
delivered out of registration order) would pass unnoticed. This pins the FULL
ordered id list: two tied at priority 5 (s-1 before s-3 by registration order)
then s-2 at priority 1 — descending priority, ties by ascending registration
order (§4.1).
#]]
  [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bus']
[?with-open [$bus:bus] $b
  [?with-open [$bus:on $b :t [?fn ($m) $m] {priority: 5}] $s1
  [?with-open [$bus:on $b :t [?fn ($m) $m] {priority: 1}] $s2
  [?with-open [$bus:on $b :t [?fn ($m) $m] {priority: 5}] $s3
    [?let [= $d [$bus:emit $b [do :t]]]
      [$map $d/fired/subscription [?fn ($x) $x@id]]]]]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
('s-1', 's-3', 's-2')
#]]
 ]
]
